commit 32f6db17e53fa1b83921af4de0996ea8f0341c35
Author: Pavlo Vynychenko <<redacted-email>>
Date:   Mon Nov 16 00:42:47 2026 +0200

    T-102: a sharp first launch, a Development build that shows what Shipping shows

    The author's first launch was blurry in Borderless. The game was not DPI
    aware, so Windows told it a 3440x1440 screen at 125% was 2752x1152 and
    stretched its picture; on top, a fresh install leaves sg.ResolutionQuality
    at 0 and TSR rendered at the engine's display-based default, about 72%.
    bAllowHighDPIInGameMode is on, and JamDisplayRules::Settle starts a first
    launch borderless at the desktop size, keeps a borderless window at the
    desktop size and renders the scene at 100% (DLSS sets its own percentage
    after it on RTX cards).

    For the jam's Development build: the F5/F6 debug keys and their hint are
    editor-only, and a packaged build turns off engine screen messages and the
    console key. -JamFrameLog=<file> writes the average frame rate.

    Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <<redacted-email>>
    Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Dd7nANeZGz4HJhvvwUv9xc

